From: OpenAI <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GDBM_File: match the old GDBM fatal callback prototype

GDBM 1.8.3 in this layer declares the fatal callback as void (*)(char *).
Match that type in Perl's compatibility callback to avoid a Werror failure.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [layer-specific GDBM 1.8.3 compatibility]

--- a/ext/GDBM_File/GDBM_File.xs
+++ b/ext/GDBM_File/GDBM_File.xs
@@ -105,14 +105,14 @@
 #elif GDBM_VERSION_MAJOR == 1 && GDBM_VERSION_MINOR >= 9
 # define FATALFUNC croak_string
 # define NEED_FATALFUNC 1
 #else
-# define FATALFUNC (void (*)()) croak_string
+# define FATALFUNC (void (*)(char *)) croak_string
 # define NEED_FATALFUNC 1
 #endif
 
 #ifdef NEED_FATALFUNC
 static void
-croak_string(const char *message) {
+croak_string(char *message) {
     Perl_croak_nocontext("%s", message);
 }
 #endif
